  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A&nbsp;ray of light passes four transparent glass slabs having&nbsp;refractive indices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. If the emergent ray <math> <mrow> <mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow> </math> is&nbsp;parallel to the incident ray <math> <mrow> <mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>,&nbsp;then&nbsp;</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0090_33edd4521a0d.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 147px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Applying Snell's law at B and C,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo></math>constant or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>sini</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mtext>&nbsp;sub&nbsp;</mtext><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0090_3b38f3a702a1.jpg\" style=\"width: 149px; height: 146px;\" /></p><p>But since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>D</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p>The Snell's law, which the students&nbsp;read in their plus two syllabus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>comes&nbsp;from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo></math>constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>sini</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>sini</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sini</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>sinr</mi></math><br /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0090_4e538b4e3adb.jpg\" style=\"width: 214px; height: 189px;\" /></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
